WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.220
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.860 --> 01:15.060
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.000 --> 01:21.560
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.340 --> 01:24.070
...is often called this...

01:24.140 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:36.720 --> 01:39.490
What do you think I am?

01:40.390 --> 01:45.160
Naoto, did you think about me
even for a little when you were leaving?

01:45.770 --> 01:47.360
Well? Naoto?

01:56.440 --> 01:57.340
Brother!

01:57.510 --> 01:59.570
Someone is going
through our memories!

02:15.260 --> 02:16.690
Damn it. Where is he?

02:21.830 --> 02:22.490
Brother!

02:23.000 --> 02:23.930
Outside!

02:24.040 --> 02:25.370
He's most likely outside!

02:30.740 --> 02:32.010
<i>Game</i>

02:32.010 --> 02:35.880
<i>Game
Episode 13</i>

02:48.760 --> 02:49.890
You're the one?

02:56.300 --> 02:59.330
What do you think I am?

02:59.910 --> 03:04.970
Naoto, did you think about me
even for a little when you were leaving?

03:10.820 --> 03:13.220
It was pretty interesting!

03:13.590 --> 03:16.110
Why don't you guys laugh too!

03:22.700 --> 03:24.750
You do such a horrible thing.

03:25.600 --> 03:30.160
If you do things like that, I don't care
what happens to that family, okay?

03:30.970 --> 03:34.770
You want me to make them run
around naked around, do you?

03:36.340 --> 03:37.870
No, Brother!

03:38.540 --> 03:40.570
He will really do it!

03:40.650 --> 03:41.980
That's right...

03:42.620 --> 03:44.670
I'll really do it!

03:44.750 --> 03:46.650
Do not lay your fingers on that family!

03:46.720 --> 03:50.590
Hey, hey, isn't it weird
if you guys take their side?

03:51.160 --> 03:53.820
You should know what they did.

03:53.890 --> 03:58.630
They committed mass murder
with mind control.

03:59.370 --> 04:04.170
Masayuki had very good qualities,
but did such a wasteful thing.

04:04.240 --> 04:06.970
Thanks to Mikuriya's lame education...

04:07.040 --> 04:10.370
...now he's not able to
use most of his power.

04:10.480 --> 04:13.710
Masayuki isn't worth using anymore.

04:13.780 --> 04:15.140
Sonezaki!

04:16.520 --> 04:19.350
You guys grew up to be fine.

04:57.420 --> 04:59.120
Oh, yeah.

04:59.330 --> 05:02.160
He is the record keeper Mr. Asano.

05:02.560 --> 05:05.030
Please look after him.

05:10.470 --> 05:11.600
Sonezaki!

05:12.270 --> 05:14.830
You killed that woman, didn't you?

05:19.750 --> 05:23.180
That woman always
wanted to commit suicide.

05:23.920 --> 05:28.050
Looking into the mirror every day
for that woman was depressing.

05:28.420 --> 05:32.360
Even then, she used a lot
of money and put on makeup...

05:32.420 --> 05:35.190
...but inside her heart, she was
always saying she wanted to die...

05:35.260 --> 05:37.460
...over and over again like a prayer.

05:38.330 --> 05:40.800
That woman liked young men.

05:40.900 --> 05:44.430
With money, she was using
many of them as her toys.

05:45.440 --> 05:48.030
It bothers me
if you misunderstand me.

05:48.340 --> 05:51.140
Even I have something
called standards, you know?

05:51.710 --> 05:52.610
Standards?

05:52.880 --> 05:57.440
The ones that I get rid of
are humans that bring about evil.

05:57.520 --> 06:01.580
It's not enough with just
the death penalty that society has.

06:02.090 --> 06:08.250
I'll tell you that the ones who stimulated
her latent complex were you guys.

06:09.090 --> 06:12.330
You guys were the ones
that killed that woman.

06:12.430 --> 06:13.520
What?

06:13.900 --> 06:16.800
Hey, instead of standing
and talking in a place like this...

06:17.170 --> 06:19.100
...why don't we have some tea?

06:21.870 --> 06:22.930
Welcome.

06:26.680 --> 06:28.910
Hey, water!

06:29.080 --> 06:30.410
Yes, right away.

06:30.520 --> 06:31.980
Hey, what's wrong?

06:32.480 --> 06:35.510
Sit down, Kirihara brothers.

06:35.820 --> 06:38.920
You think we are in any mood
to sit down with you and have tea?

06:39.690 --> 06:42.090
Then just feel that way.

06:42.460 --> 06:44.860
You have no choice
but to feel that way.

06:54.770 --> 06:57.670
Oh no, Takashi!
What happened to your face?

06:58.640 --> 07:00.270
My gosh, come on!

07:12.020 --> 07:13.960
Wipe it off. Here.

07:17.830 --> 07:18.690
You...

07:18.760 --> 07:20.460
Hey, hey...

07:20.670 --> 07:22.860
Watch how you talk to me!

07:33.980 --> 07:35.140
Brother...

07:38.720 --> 07:41.780
You should have just
done that from the beginning.

07:42.490 --> 07:44.920
Is it fun doing such a thing?

07:45.220 --> 07:46.350
Brother...

07:46.930 --> 07:49.120
Is coffee fine with you?

07:50.160 --> 07:53.060
Your cute little brother wants...

07:53.670 --> 07:55.290
...melon soda, huh?

07:56.740 --> 08:01.700
You have a memory you can't say
much about with melon soda, right?

08:05.110 --> 08:08.480
"Creases in your heart"
is a good phrase.

08:09.150 --> 08:11.480
If there's something that's
stuck with you in your memory...

08:11.550 --> 08:14.490
...that will be made
into an image in your head.

08:14.590 --> 08:19.420
If you do that,
that comes jumping right into me.

08:21.590 --> 08:24.650
Those things you call
creases in your heart...

08:24.730 --> 08:26.960
Hey, three coffees please.

08:27.030 --> 08:28.730
Yes, I understand.

08:38.810 --> 08:39.670
Stop it!

08:45.420 --> 08:46.610
Please!

08:46.690 --> 08:48.020
Make them stop...

08:53.190 --> 08:58.530
That woman was betrayed
by this guy so many times.

08:59.060 --> 09:01.970
So she actually wanted to do this.

09:02.030 --> 09:03.800
How pitiful...

09:04.200 --> 09:08.040
She didn't want to break up,
so she's held it in for so long.

09:08.110 --> 09:09.270
That's horrible.

09:09.510 --> 09:10.740
You...

09:10.810 --> 09:12.830
...killed Tsukasa Kamiya, huh?

09:18.920 --> 09:24.050
Yeah, because that guy's
job was already over.

09:24.160 --> 09:25.320
And...

09:25.920 --> 09:27.260
...you tried to kill me too.

09:33.570 --> 09:36.630
You were the one that was
at the research lab that time.

09:37.070 --> 09:40.130
That was something like an ability test.

09:40.740 --> 09:44.230
I'll tell you now that we
won't go as you want us to be.

09:44.440 --> 09:45.740
Thank you for waiting.

09:45.980 --> 09:47.310
Hey...

09:47.410 --> 09:49.240
Naoto Kirihara.

09:49.750 --> 09:54.080
You know how the good guy
beats up the bad guy, right?

09:54.450 --> 09:58.450
When I see things like that,
I always think this...

10:01.260 --> 10:04.890
The good guy can't win, right?

10:05.160 --> 10:09.160
The good guy has
too many things he can't do.

10:09.400 --> 10:14.840
But to the bad guys, there isn't a
single thing they aren't allowed to do.

10:15.310 --> 10:17.240
That's why there's
no way they can win.

10:17.310 --> 10:19.000
There's too much of a handicap.

10:19.080 --> 10:20.740
I brought you another cup.

10:24.050 --> 10:28.180
There isn't a single thing
I'm not allowed to do.

10:28.790 --> 10:32.120
So that's why you guys
can't win against me.

10:32.290 --> 10:36.350
You have to listen to me.
There is no other way.

10:37.660 --> 10:39.790
Regardless of what
that girl does to you...

10:39.870 --> 10:42.430
...you can't do anything, right?

10:46.540 --> 10:48.170
I brought you another cup.

10:52.880 --> 10:54.810
Think about it hard.

10:55.710 --> 10:58.150
You guys are the same way.

10:58.650 --> 11:01.620
Thanks to you guys
being at Mikuriya's...

11:01.690 --> 11:05.180
...you guys made the mistake
of using your own powers...

11:05.260 --> 11:08.120
...to become material
for an inferiority complex.

11:09.360 --> 11:11.420
Inferiority complex...

11:12.000 --> 11:16.370
...why don't you throw something
like that into the garbage can...

11:16.440 --> 11:18.230
...just like your dark memories!

11:18.400 --> 11:20.200
Why do you
associate yourself with us!

11:20.270 --> 11:22.540
Because I can't watch you guys.

11:23.140 --> 11:26.010
You guys are pretty horrible.

11:27.180 --> 11:28.700
Look at me.

11:29.180 --> 11:31.840
My life is my stage.

11:32.380 --> 11:34.580
Boring dramas
will never be able to top it!

11:34.650 --> 11:37.210
My acting was wonderful, right?

11:37.920 --> 11:41.020
This kind of wonderful drama
doesn't exist anywhere else!

11:42.630 --> 11:44.290
What happened to the research lab?

11:46.130 --> 11:47.220
I don't know...

11:48.170 --> 11:52.400
You guys wasted 15 years
of your life by being there for him.

11:52.470 --> 11:57.000
It shouldn't matter to you guys
what happens to Mikuriya.

11:57.440 --> 11:59.410
You should have been there too.

11:59.850 --> 12:01.610
I've seen your file before.

12:10.490 --> 12:14.650
I thought Elder Misaki
was just a keeper.

12:15.690 --> 12:19.960
I didn't know that old man
had powers to put a barrier up.

12:20.770 --> 12:24.430
I was locked up
in there for three years.

12:24.840 --> 12:27.200
You were saved by Mr. Mikuriya.

12:27.910 --> 12:31.030
If Mr. Mikuriya didn't save you,
destruction would most likely...

12:32.540 --> 12:34.240
Naoya Kirihara!

12:34.750 --> 12:37.150
You went into my consciousness,
didn't you?

12:37.220 --> 12:39.910
It's because you
remembered the research lab.

12:40.620 --> 12:44.060
Meaning even I have something
called a crease in my heart, huh?

12:53.400 --> 12:54.590
Why don't you die!

12:54.670 --> 12:55.890
What did you say!

12:55.970 --> 12:57.260
Try saying it one more time!

12:57.370 --> 12:58.700
I will... I will! I will!

12:58.770 --> 13:00.400
I'll say it as many times as possible!

13:00.470 --> 13:01.340
What!

13:02.240 --> 13:04.440
You're such a slob!

13:04.680 --> 13:06.270
You have no right to say that to me!

13:06.340 --> 13:10.680
If you were a man, you would think
of the family more, don't you think?

13:13.590 --> 13:14.920
You kicked me!

13:15.650 --> 13:18.380
You hit your husband? What a slut!

13:22.360 --> 13:24.390
Everyone, just die!

13:24.530 --> 13:25.760
Why don't you die!

13:26.100 --> 13:27.030
Damn it...

13:30.840 --> 13:32.460
Do you want to ask him too?

13:32.540 --> 13:34.840
Sonezaki is so down,
so I don't like him!

13:34.910 --> 13:35.770
Right?

13:35.840 --> 13:37.540
Leave a guy like him alone.

13:41.810 --> 13:42.970
Stupid idiot!

13:43.080 --> 13:44.210
What are you doing!

13:45.180 --> 13:46.050
Hey!

13:46.120 --> 13:47.950
This isn't something for you to watch!

13:48.950 --> 13:51.550
Hey, what the hell
are you doing, damn it!

13:51.760 --> 13:52.550
Ouch!

13:52.860 --> 13:54.790
Please forgive me, Brother!

13:55.160 --> 13:57.150
Hey, hey, come on. Get up!

13:58.160 --> 14:00.430
Forgive me. It hurts...

14:00.670 --> 14:01.930
It doesn't hurt.

14:02.300 --> 14:04.270
Something like that doesn't hurt.

14:04.670 --> 14:06.830
It doesn't hurt. Counterattack him.

14:10.640 --> 14:12.080
Counterattack him!

14:12.410 --> 14:14.000
Kill that man!

14:14.310 --> 14:15.510
Kill him!

14:20.050 --> 14:21.210
That's right.

14:21.290 --> 14:22.750
Do it. Do it.

14:22.820 --> 14:24.080
Don't hold back.

14:27.630 --> 14:28.520
That's right!

14:29.030 --> 14:31.000
Punch him! Keep on punching him!

14:31.060 --> 14:33.220
Don't hold back!

14:35.300 --> 14:37.230
Both of you, die!

14:37.740 --> 14:39.900
Let's make this end here.

14:41.840 --> 14:44.970
Let's make your
lonesome suffering end here.

14:45.140 --> 14:46.200
Who are you?

14:46.410 --> 14:47.810
Doesn't matter who I am.

14:48.580 --> 14:51.110
I came here to save you.

14:58.620 --> 15:02.650
Didn't you throw out your
dark past in a garbage can?

15:02.760 --> 15:04.420
Shut up.

15:04.700 --> 15:07.390
The one that saved me
wasn't Mikuriya.

15:07.900 --> 15:09.760
It's not Misaki either.

15:10.770 --> 15:15.300
Misaki gave up on
keeping me in confinement.

15:16.310 --> 15:17.830
He abandoned me.

15:17.910 --> 15:21.740
That's why I was able to get out.

15:21.880 --> 15:24.250
Then who saved you?

15:24.880 --> 15:27.910
You guys would be saved too.

15:28.390 --> 15:30.680
No, I'll save you.

15:31.620 --> 15:35.150
Aren't you going to just make us
subordinates and use us as you please?

15:35.430 --> 15:37.620
Babble on, loser.

15:38.260 --> 15:40.360
You aren't fun.

15:40.900 --> 15:42.490
You aren't having fun.

15:42.570 --> 15:43.560
What?

15:43.800 --> 15:46.740
There is no happiness
in a battle without struggle.

15:47.270 --> 15:50.070
You know that the opponent
is going to resign.

15:50.140 --> 15:52.300
There is no exciting feeling at all...

15:52.380 --> 15:55.540
...to keep on creating the drama
that you know the ending to!

15:56.650 --> 15:57.580
Naoya...

15:57.650 --> 15:59.550
Y-You...

15:59.950 --> 16:02.110
That's what you are thinking.

16:06.590 --> 16:07.890
May I help you?

16:08.030 --> 16:09.790
These guys are...

16:10.030 --> 16:11.000
Yes.

16:20.340 --> 16:21.170
Stop it!

16:24.780 --> 16:25.770
What!

16:27.750 --> 16:29.480
Stop it! It's painful!

16:30.120 --> 16:31.740
Let go, Saori!

16:32.680 --> 16:33.910
It's really painful!

16:33.990 --> 16:36.390
You thought I didn't know about it?

16:36.450 --> 16:38.450
S-Saori...

16:38.690 --> 16:39.120
Stop!

16:39.120 --> 16:39.560
Stop!
If you move...

16:39.560 --> 16:40.220
If you move...

16:40.290 --> 16:42.450
...it will become worse.

16:48.100 --> 16:49.330
I like you...

16:49.530 --> 16:50.730
I like you very much...

16:50.970 --> 16:52.130
I love you...

16:52.600 --> 16:53.760
Me too.

16:54.110 --> 16:56.230
I also love you.

16:56.780 --> 16:57.740
I'm so happy.

17:06.520 --> 17:09.450
Okay, then why don't
we go with the take?

17:12.220 --> 17:14.560
Did you see on the internet?

17:14.630 --> 17:15.130
The porn video?

17:15.130 --> 17:16.530
The porn video?
Isn't that her?

17:16.590 --> 17:18.060
No way! Why?

17:18.230 --> 17:19.030
Isn't that her?

17:19.100 --> 17:21.790
What did you do!

17:22.600 --> 17:25.230
Everyone in town knows about it!

17:25.570 --> 17:26.730
You!

17:26.970 --> 17:28.170
I want to run.

17:28.340 --> 17:29.970
I can't believe anyone.

17:30.380 --> 17:32.140
I want to run away from here.

17:32.340 --> 17:34.210
I want to run away!

17:42.550 --> 17:45.790
That's punishment
for coming into my heart.

17:51.260 --> 17:52.030
You!

17:52.030 --> 17:53.550
You!
Naoto Kirihara!

17:54.030 --> 17:56.630
You still don't get it, do you?

17:57.700 --> 18:02.610
There isn't one thing that I can't do!

18:04.580 --> 18:08.100
Regardless of what happens,
it's all you guys' fault.

18:08.550 --> 18:09.770
Naoto!

18:12.620 --> 18:16.020
Do you think it's okay leaving
the world up to all those humans...

18:16.090 --> 18:19.550
...with their consciousnesses
running about freely?

18:21.360 --> 18:25.990
After all, most of these guys aren't
really thinking of anything on their own!

18:26.530 --> 18:30.400
They mistake what's been forced
upon them for what they selected...

18:30.470 --> 18:32.730
...as they keep on being exploited!

18:32.800 --> 18:34.400
Isn't that right?

18:34.470 --> 18:38.970
If you let those guys all of a sudden
have their own self-assertion...

18:39.040 --> 18:41.910
...this world won't have
anything good coming!

18:42.180 --> 18:44.270
This world will be destroyed!

18:44.350 --> 18:47.440
Hey, those that were trampled down!

18:47.520 --> 18:52.220
Why don't we fire up this world
with wonderful music from the body!

18:52.290 --> 18:54.020
Hallelujah!

18:56.130 --> 18:58.030
There's no way
reformation is coming!

18:58.100 --> 19:03.090
Humans loves material civilization!
The fine living surrounded by things.

19:03.170 --> 19:04.970
The value of everything
is chosen with money!

19:05.040 --> 19:06.970
They love that kind of world!

19:07.040 --> 19:09.060
They love to defeat people!

19:09.140 --> 19:11.110
They love to bully!

19:11.180 --> 19:13.540
They love to betray!

19:15.150 --> 19:18.080
Not a single one of them is thinking
about anything but themselves!

19:18.150 --> 19:24.350
Those that talk about love, if they're
forced into a corner, they hurt people!

19:24.890 --> 19:26.360
Isn't that right?

19:26.860 --> 19:28.950
They love to kill people!

19:29.090 --> 19:31.120
They love wars!

19:31.200 --> 19:32.890
Bang! Ba-bang!

19:33.130 --> 19:35.070
Bang! Bazoom!

19:35.130 --> 19:36.960
There's no way
reformation is coming!

19:37.040 --> 19:38.830
Isn't that right, CEO?

19:39.140 --> 19:40.660
The great predictor!

19:41.140 --> 19:46.600
You said that, so that's why
I decided to believe you!

19:46.680 --> 19:48.010
Yo, yo!

19:48.380 --> 19:50.940
Yo! Yo, yo!

20:03.090 --> 20:04.120
Ark...

20:08.370 --> 20:10.030
Reiko was saying...

20:10.100 --> 20:13.970
...A- A-Ark was chasing after her.

20:15.310 --> 20:16.470
Ark?

20:17.510 --> 20:19.440
And I see a desert...

20:21.310 --> 20:23.870
There is a girl
standing in the desert.

20:24.180 --> 20:25.270
Shouko?

20:29.290 --> 20:30.380
Ark...

20:31.420 --> 20:33.120
What is Ark?

20:35.160 --> 20:36.220
Ark?

20:41.570 --> 20:42.830
You...

20:45.870 --> 20:47.240
Oh...

20:47.310 --> 20:49.770
I see it. The demon's powers...

20:49.840 --> 20:51.780
I can see it!

21:20.270 --> 21:22.070
Wonderful!

21:22.140 --> 21:23.940
It's really wonderful!

21:24.480 --> 21:27.340
You guys are seriously wonderful!

21:28.080 --> 21:32.380
You guys are making my heart
excited for the first time in a while.

21:32.720 --> 21:35.050
You let me enjoy...

21:35.350 --> 21:39.290
I see. This is what
they meant by uncertain data.

21:40.160 --> 21:42.890
Naoto Kirihara and Naoya Kirihara...

21:42.960 --> 21:46.590
Welcome to my boring life.

21:47.630 --> 21:50.030
This is the end of the first act.

21:55.970 --> 21:56.870
Wait...

21:58.610 --> 21:59.540
Brother!

22:11.860 --> 22:13.410
Brother, this is bad.

22:13.490 --> 22:14.920
The research lab...

22:15.460 --> 22:17.550
The research lab is on fire.

22:17.960 --> 22:21.860
Mr. Mikuriya is seeking our help!

22:31.240 --> 22:34.510
<i>An exact answer is nowhere.</i>

22:34.580 --> 22:37.170
<i>Even if you corner it, it still runs.</i>

22:37.250 --> 22:41.840
<i>It's that kind of repeating all the time.</i>

22:41.920 --> 22:45.150
<i>We hurt each other
and rip each other apart.</i>

22:45.220 --> 22:47.850
<i>We're complaining once again.</i>

22:47.930 --> 22:53.260
<i>When tomorrow comes, just like a lie,
you wear a mask and live on.</i>

22:53.330 --> 22:58.630
<i>I was wishing upon
the night stars...</i>

22:58.700 --> 23:03.970
<i>... for our distance
to become shorter.</i>

23:04.040 --> 23:10.680
<i>But if I try to bluff,
then I'm going to regret it.</i>

23:10.750 --> 23:13.220
<i>Words and feelings are reverse.</i>

23:13.280 --> 23:18.850
<i>Feelings that were asleep,
heart that was asleep, lure it out!</i>

23:18.920 --> 23:24.190
<i>Glamour that was asleep, myself
that was asleep, with your power!</i>

23:24.260 --> 23:29.720
<i>Please look at me quietly with the soul
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:29.800 --> 23:34.600
<i>I want you to go wilder inside me.</i>

23:34.670 --> 23:40.130
<i>Eyes that were asleep, emotions
that were asleep, wake them up!</i>

23:40.210 --> 23:45.480
<i>Memories that were asleep, dreams
that were asleep, with your power!</i>

23:45.550 --> 23:51.010
<i>Please melt me with the vision of kindness
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:51.090 --> 23:58.190
<i>I want to stay asleep
longer buried inside you.</i>

24:01.000 --> 24:03.300
The closed land of memories...

24:03.630 --> 24:05.690
...which has turned into
a mound of black rubble.

24:07.040 --> 24:11.300
It's a place filled with memories
of hatred and disappointment.

24:12.310 --> 24:15.680
The awkward reunion
accelerated the revolt...

24:16.410 --> 24:18.940
...as the ill feeling that
has lost its outlet...

24:19.320 --> 24:22.580
...makes myself
go out to the battlefield.

24:23.450 --> 24:29.860
<i>Episode 14, "Confinement"</i>

24:26.120 --> 24:28.530
Where are we headed?
